<Legal title="Accessibility Statement" heading="Accessibility Statement" description="Swarmnest's accessibility goals, known limitations and how to report an accessibility problem." path="/accessibility/">
<p>We want swarmnest.ai to be usable by everyone, including people who use screen readers, keyboard navigation, magnification or other assistive technology.</p>

<h2>Our Goal</h2>
<p>We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. We have not yet had an independent audit, so we do not claim full conformance.</p>

<h2>What We Do</h2>
<ul>
<li>Simple, text-first pages with semantic HTML headings, lists, tables and labelled form fields.</li>
<li>Pages that work without JavaScript for reading the directory, and that adapt to light and dark mode settings.</li>
<li>Machine-readable versions of the directory (JSON, <code>llms.txt</code>) for people who prefer to use their own tools or assistants to read it.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Known Limitations</h2>
<ul>
<li>Our waitlist sign-up currently opens your email app instead of an on-page form.</li>
<li>Checkout pages, when live, are provided by Stripe, and linked third-party sites are outside our control.</li>
<li>Some downloadable products may include files from third-party tools (for example workflow exports) whose accessibility depends on those tools.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Tell Us About a Problem</h2>
<p>If something is hard to use, email <a href="mailto:hello@swarmnest.ai?subject=Accessibility">hello@swarmnest.ai</a> with the subject "Accessibility", the page URL, and what happened (including your browser and assistive technology, if you like). We aim to reply within 5 business days, and can provide information or product details in another format on request.</p>
</Legal>
